WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.517
Our capstone has ten design requirements.

2
00:00:02.637 --> 00:00:06.179
Eight have adequate design evidence; two
remain open.

3
00:00:06.299 --> 00:00:10.651
The arithmetic coverage is 80%, but there
is no eighty-percent

4
00:00:10.771 --> 00:00:12.648
DQ acceptance threshold.

5
00:00:12.768 --> 00:00:16.395
The first gap concerns an unspecified
contact gasket.

6
00:00:16.515 --> 00:00:20.888
The second concerns an unproven response
to a shared sensor failure.

7
00:00:21.008 --> 00:00:24.955
The diagram deliberately puts the coverage
bar beside the gaps.

8
00:00:25.075 --> 00:00:29.064
A high completion percentage does not
remove the importance of

9
00:00:29.184 --> 00:00:30.476
what is missing.

10
00:00:31.096 --> 00:00:36.024
The supported conclusion is that this
package does not justify routine use

11
00:00:36.144 --> 00:00:40.198
or a complete favourable design conclusion
for the affected scope.

12
00:00:40.318 --> 00:00:44.627
Some limited work may continue only
through the applicable documented

13
00:00:44.747 --> 00:00:46.731
assessment and authorization.

14
00:00:46.851 --> 00:00:50.783
Ask what activity is proposed and whether
the gaps could affect it.

15
00:00:50.903 --> 00:00:54.444
Do not approve a blank category called
conditional release.

16
00:00:54.564 --> 00:00:59.535
Name the activity, restrictions,
responsible decision-maker and conditions

17
00:00:59.655 --> 00:01:01.234
that must be met first.

18
00:01:01.854 --> 00:01:06.163
Prepare a handover containing the accepted
design baseline, reviewed

19
00:01:06.283 --> 00:01:10.827
requirements, risk/control rationale,
open-action register and

20
00:01:10.947 --> 00:01:12.696
planned verification links.

21
00:01:12.816 --> 00:01:17.510
Installation qualification will need the
correct drawings, specifications

22
00:01:17.630 --> 00:01:19.358
and component identities.

23
00:01:19.478 --> 00:01:23.979
Unresolved design choices should not
disappear into a signature page.

24
00:01:24.099 --> 00:01:28.664
Identify which installation activities
depend on closing each gap.

25
00:01:28.784 --> 00:01:33.371
This creates a practical connection to
Module 4 rather than implying that

26
00:01:33.491 --> 00:01:36.951
the next stage starts simply because this
course has ended.

27
00:01:37.571 --> 00:01:40.792
Your final task is to write a short
decision memo.

28
00:01:40.912 --> 00:01:44.906
State what was reviewed, what the evidence
supports, which important

29
00:01:45.026 --> 00:01:47.970
questions remain and what action is
required.

30
00:01:48.090 --> 00:01:52.399
Explain why the completion percentage does
not determine suitability.

31
00:01:52.519 --> 00:01:55.748
Compare your memo with the worked answer,
then take the

32
00:01:55.868 --> 00:01:57.742
separate application assessment.

33
00:01:57.862 --> 00:02:00.784
Course completion is self-study evidence
only.

34
00:02:00.904 --> 00:02:05.662
It does not replace supervised experience,
an independent technical review

35
00:02:05.782 --> 00:02:08.918
or authorization to perform regulated
work.
